    <h1 class="text-3xl md:text-4xl font-bold text-theme-primary mb-4">
      Wire Mesh Shipping &amp; Packaging: How It Arrives Undamaged
    </h1>

    <p class="text-theme-secondary text-lg mb-8">
      Last updated: September 2026 | 11 min read
    </p>

    <!-- Answer First -->
    <div class="bg-theme-card border border-theme rounded-lg p-6 mb-8">
      <p class="text-theme-primary text-lg leading-relaxed">
        <strong>Quick answer:</strong> Wire mesh arrives undamaged when you specify the packing before production, not after. The essentials: <strong>rolls</strong> ship wrapped in waterproof kraft paper (min 80 g/m²) plus a woven polypropylene bag, strapped with 4–6 steel or PET bands, on end or flat-stacked with dunnage between layers; <strong>panels and welded mesh sheets</strong> ship on fumigated ISPM-15 wooden pallets, banded and edge-protected, wrapped in stretch film plus a moisture barrier for sea freight. For any ocean shipment over ~20 days, add VCI paper or desiccant strips inside the wrap and specify container condensation control. Then photograph everything at loading and at unpacking—the photo record is what makes a damage claim winnable.
      </p>
    </div>

    <!-- TOC -->
    <div class="bg-theme-card border border-theme rounded-lg p-6 mb-8">
      <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-theme-primary mb-4">Table of Contents</h2>
      <ul class="space-y-2 text-theme-secondary">
        <li><a href="#roll-vs-panel" class="hover:text-theme-primary">Roll vs Panel Packing: What to Specify</a></li>
        <li><a href="#moisture" class="hover:text-theme-primary">Moisture and Corrosion Protection for Sea Freight</a></li>
        <li><a href="#strapping" class="hover:text-theme-primary">Strapping, Pallets, and Labeling Norms</a></li>
        <li><a href="#loading" class="hover:text-theme-primary">Container Loading Patterns for Wire Mesh</a></li>
        <li><a href="#claims" class="hover:text-theme-primary">Receiving Inspection and the Damage Claims Process</a></li>
        <li><a href="#faq" class="hover:text-theme-primary">FAQ</a></li>
      </ul>
